noah bedford wrote:

>>How much ram, how much flash memory would a phone need for nethack?
> 
> That isn't the problem... it is that most phones use ARM chips,
> or some other portable architecture, and I do not think nethack
> has been ported to those yet. 

The original Symbian port runs on a Psion 5 (or a Revo) with 8Mb RAM, and 
no flash memory. However, I'm not sure whether you could ascend on that 
without running out of filesystem space. Add a 16Mb flash card and it was 
certainly be possible. A 5MX (16Mb RAM) runs Nethack fairly happily.

All of the above use ARM processors, either 18MHz or 36MHz: the CPU speed 
is not generally an issue with nethack.

Screen resolution is generally a bigger problem. To fit the map on screen 
on a revo requires a ridiculously small font, and even a 5/5MX (640x240 
pixels) isn't good. Yes, you can use a larger font and scroll, but nethack 
works best if you don't.

Keyboard is the other issue. You need a good keyboard for the game to be 
reasonably playable.


